    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n12665" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dē-fēnĕro</span></b> ,
			āvi, ātum, 1, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>v. a., to involve in
				debt</i>, <i><span class="en">Ambros. de Tobia
			9</span></i>.—Hence, <i>P. a.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dēfēnĕrātus</span></b> ,
				a, um, <i>overwhelmed by debt,
				exhausted by usury</i> (post-class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">plurimis creditoribus defeneratus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. Mag. p. 322, 21</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Ambros. Ep. 7, 1</span></i>.</div>
